Well, you may want to consider how long it has taken me to get to "ally" with both Kromzek and Kromrif before you decide to go this route.  I estimate that I've spent somewhere in the neighborhood of 40 hours in-game time getting my faction to where it is now, and I'm *still* only up to dubious with Tormax.  I'm pretty sure the vast majority of quest giving giants are on Kromrif and Kromzek faction, but it took me around 30 hours worth of work to be able to get some quests.  Tormax faction is a serious pain in the rear to gain if you aren't doing raids on Icewell Keep or deep into Skyshrine.  <P>Now, if you can handle doing that kinda faction work, then I honestly think that Giant is the way to go.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0">  Admitedly, I may NEVER get to do any of the armor quests, but since I go on PoG raids anyway, that doesn't bother me.  The fact that I don't have to worry about invis dropping on my way thru kael to PoG, or Skyshrine, or a ton of other places, is key for me.  Thurgadin is out of the way of just about everything, and you never have to run through there to get anyplace.  Skyshrine is a nice short easy run if you are on your way to CS or further west.  <P>A lot of the mobs that I've been killing for faction, sentries and guardians in skyshrine for kromzek (storm giants), and coldain for kromzek AND kromrif (frost giants), would still give exp to people in their 40's.  Almost all of them are green at 54, but i'm getting enough exp and faction to keep me interested in killing them.  Dobbin Crossaxe won't go green until I hit 56, so farming him for faction, exp, and coldain heads isn't too bad.  So, if anyone wants to join me for faction work, just let me know.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>--------------------<P>Lownar Baardeth - 54th Level Gnecromancer<BR>Kalaan - 30th Level Rogue<BR>Bertox. Server<P>Sendil- 50th Level Rogue<BR>Solusek Ro Server
